  "body": "## Description\nWhen tasks are submitted with an AbortSignal and the pool is busy, tasks are moved to skipQueue instead of taskQueue. The queueSize getter was incorrectly including skipQueue.length in its calculation.\n\n## Fix\nqueueSize now only reflects `taskQueue.size - pendingCapacity`, matching the expected behavior where skipQueue tasks (rejected due to pool being busy with AbortSignal) are not counted as \"queued\".\n\n## Changes\n- `src/index.ts`: Updated queueSize getter to exclude skipQueue from count\n\n## Testing\nReproduced the bug: with maxThreads=1 and maxQueue=1, submitting 10 tasks with AbortSignal and then aborting showed queueSize=8 incorrectly immediately after abort. After fix, queueSize correctly reflects only taskQueue items.\n\nFixes #1029",
